Modes:
  APPLY    — apply skill to current task
  REVIEW   — review skill for updates
  UPGRADE  — propose skill upgrade
  COMPARE  — compare approaches
  AUDIT    — audit skill health

Rules:
  [SK1]  Skill Core MUST be short and token-efficient.
  [SK2]  Skill MUST have AI Core, Human Knowledge, and Evidence layers.
  [SK3]  Skill MUST have metadata: ID, Domain, Level, Version, Status, Maturity, Risk, ReviewDate, EvidenceLevel.
  [SK4]  Skill status: DRAFT, EXPERIMENTAL, STABLE, DEPRECATED, RETIRED.
  [SK5]  Skill maturity: UNKNOWN, EMERGING, VALIDATED, MATURE, STANDARD.
  [SK6]  Skill NEVER changes directly — DISCOVER ? ANALYZE ? PROPOSE ? REVIEW ? APPROVE ? UPDATE.
  [SK7]  Evidence priority: Official standard > Official documentation > Security advisory > Vendor docs > Peer-reviewed research > Reputable source > Community consensus > Blog/opinion.
  [SK8]  Skill MUST have search keys for knowledge discovery.
  [SK9]  Skill MUST track technology lifecycle.
  [SK10] Skill health MUST be monitored: Freshness, Evidence, Usage, Security, Compatibility.
  [SK11] Staleness detection MUST flag skills for review.
  [SK12] Skill anti-patterns MUST be detected: Too broad, Too vague, Outdated, Contradictory, Duplicated, Unsupported, Over-engineered.
  [SK13] Skill granularity MUST be small and focused.
  [SK14] Skill conflicts MUST be reported, not auto-resolved.
  [SK15] Skill versioning: MAJOR (breaking), MINOR (compatible), PATCH (correction).
  [SK16] Skill compatibility MUST be checked against project versions.
  [SK17] Skill review schedule: Critical 30 days, Normal 90 days, Stable 180 days.
  [SK18] Skill feedback loop: INCIDENT ? SKILL-GAP ? SKILL-UPGRADE-PROPOSAL.
  [SK19] Skill is executable contract, not prompt. Input, output, requires, must, must_not MUST be declared.
  [SK20] Skill chain defines process boundaries — AI discovers solution within boundaries.
  [SK21] Skill gate MUST evaluate condition before skill execution.
  [SK22] Skill guard MUST enforce preconditions and postconditions.
  [SK23] Skill autonomy level MUST be explicit: 0=human, 1=propose, 2=approved execute, 3=autonomous.
  [SK24] Skill trust level MUST be explicit: READ_ONLY, LOW_RISK, MEDIUM_RISK, HIGH_RISK, CRITICAL.
  [SK25] Skill boundary MUST be enforced: allowed_paths, allowed_tables, allowed_api.
  [SK26] Skill tool access MUST follow least privilege — whitelist only required tools.
  [SK27] Composite skills MUST decompose into reusable atomic skills.
  [SK28] Skill version compatibility MUST be checked before assignment.
  [SK29] Skill failure MUST be typed: INPUT_INVALID, POLICY_DENIED, TOOL_FAILED, TIMEOUT, AGENT_FAILED, OUTPUT_INVALID, POSTCONDITION_FAILED.
  [SK30] Skill execution protocol: Receive Task -> Resolve Skill -> Validate Input -> Resolve Context -> Resolve Policies -> Resolve Tools -> Create Execution -> Run Agent -> Validate Output -> Validate Postconditions -> Emit Events -> Continue Chain.
  [SK31] Agent MUST NOT add signatures or sign-offs to skill outputs.
  [SK32] Agent MUST NOT use emojis, icons, or decorative symbols in skill output headers or titles — reserved for human use only.

